#. ~ Description of furniture "green algae"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid "A short patch of grassy green seaweed, wholly unremarkable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "sugar kelp"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid ""
"Also known as kombu, this brown algae grows in a single leaflike blade that "
"can reach more than twice the height of a man.  Young fronds make for "
"excellent soup stock and can even be eaten raw."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "sea sponge"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid ""
"An immobile, lumpy little creature that looks nothing like a square kitchen "
"sponge.  Anchored to the sea floor, its porous body passively filters "
"plankton from the water that freely passes through it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "bladderwrack"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid ""
"Named for the air bladders that grow all over its leafy fronds, this leafy "
"seaweed is technically edible and has a long history of use in folk "
"medicine."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "red algae"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid ""
"One of the thousands of species of grassy reddish marine plants that inhabit"
" intertidal zones the world over.  Its rubbery little fronds don't look "
"particularly edible."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "sea lettuce"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid ""
"Sometimes known as green laver, this leafy algae from the Ulva genus grows "
"in leafy little patches around shallows and tide pools.  Though small, it "
"makes a tasty snack."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of furniture "sea anemone"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
msgid ""
"This sessile polyp waves its stinging tentacles with the motion of the "
"tides, hoping to capture a tiny fish or crab.  It's wholly inedible and "
"poses no danger to anything bigger than a shrimp."
msgstr ""

