"weapon uses a system of three different magazines to field 15 12-gauge "
"shotgun shells within a comparatively compact design.  As the weapon's "
"trigger assembly is situated forwards of the chamber and magazines in what "
"is termed as a 'bullpup' design, the firearm's notably more compact than its"
" peers despite having a higher capacity when compared against more "
"classically designed shotguns."
