#. ~ Description of "foam rubber bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A baseball bat made of foam rubber with a plastic handle.  Light and easy to"
" wield, but almost completely ineffective if your goal is to hurt someone."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "nail bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A baseball bat with several nails driven through it.  The spikes look "
"dangerous, but they're sure to make it less durable."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "barbed wire bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A baseball bat wrapped with barbed wire, giving it a little extra oomph "
"without compromising its durability."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "soaking stone war club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A curved wooden club cradling a stone head.  It is currently soaking in oil "
"and won't be properly fit for combat for a while longer."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "stone war club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A curved wooden club cradling a stone head.  These weapons were once used by"
" indigenous peoples across North America."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "soaking wooden war club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A curved wooden club with a ball head carved from a root burl.  These "
"devastating weapons were once used by indigenous peoples across North "
"America."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wooden war club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A curved wooden club with a ball head carved from a root burl.  These "
"weapons were once used by indigenous peoples across North America."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "hockey stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A curved wooden stick with with a flat paddle at one end, commonly used by "
"hockey players."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A fighting staff carved out of wood.  Lightweight and good for defense, it "
"is surprisingly easy to handle."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tooth-bladed macuahuitl"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A flat wooden club with impossibly-sharp teeth stuck to both sides, a "
"postapocalyptic facsimile of the weapons once used by Aztec warriors."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "glass-bladed macuahuitl"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A flat wooden club with sharpened flakes of stone, ceramic, or glass stuck "
"to both sides, a reasonable facsimile of the weapons once used by Aztec "
"warriors."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tonfa"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A hard plastic truncheon commonly employed by police.  Originally an "
"Okinawan weapon, it consists of a stick with a perpendicular handle attached"
" a third of the way down its length."
msgstr "一根通常被警察所使用的硬塑膠製短棍。源自沖繩的武器， 由一個握柄垂直連結於棍子的三分之一處所組成。"

#. ~ Description of "pool cue"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A hardwood stick designed for hitting colorful balls around a felt table.  "
"Truly, the coolest of sports."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "sledgehammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A heavy steel head on a long shaft, designed for demolition work.  It's a "
"very hard-hitting melee weapon, but slow to swing and will probably exhaust "
"you quickly."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "nail board"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A hefty plank of wood.  The nails driven through one end look nasty enough, "
"but it remains a very awkward weapon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "Mjölnir"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A large hammer, forged from the heart of a dying star.  It bears the inscription:\n"
"\n"
"Whosoever holds this hammer,\n"
"If he be worthy,\n"
"Shall possess the power to…\n"
"CRUSH!'"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "ironshod quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A long wooden staff reinforced with steel langets and ferrules."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "walking stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A long, thin stick carved smooth for an easy grip.  These are commonly used "
"by hikers to help navigate steep slopes, and could serve as a fighting "
"staff, though this one looks too thin to last for long."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "war hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval hammer with a spike on one end, made for battle.  Its odd shape "
"and balance make it an excellent weapon, but an ineffective tool."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "morningstar"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a spiked metal ball on "
"the end.  It is bigger and heavier than a typical mace, and its spikes can "
"deal serious damage to soft targets."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wooden handle with a knob-shaped steel "
"head."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "steel bladed macuahuitl"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A modern reimagining of the ancient Aztec weapon, made of a flat wooden club"
" inset along its edges with steel razor blades."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "aluminum crutches"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A pair of aluminum rods with a brace and padding designed to help support "
"the body using the arms.  These would make for an abysmal weapon, but they'd"
" help you get around on a broken leg."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "mismatched crutches"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A pair of rods, one wood and one aluminum, with braces designed to help "
"support the body using the arms.  These would make for an abysmal weapon, "
"but they'd help you get around on a broken leg."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wooden crutches"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A pair of wooden rods with a brace designed to help support the body using "
"the arms.  These would make for an abysmal weapon, but they'd help you get "
"around on a broken leg."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of variant "plastic wizard cane" of item "plastic toy cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A plastic cane designed to look like a wizard's staff.  They shall not pass!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of variant "plastic fairy wand" of item "plastic toy cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A plastic cane festooned with ribbons and glitter."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tactical tonfa (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A reinforced plastic tonfa; the core is filled with capacitors and a high-"
"yield rechargeable storage battery.  When a switch on the handle is pressed,"
" a high-voltage current is transmitted to the two electrodes mounted in the "
"end of the tonfa, and by extension to anyone unfortunate enough to be in "
"contact with them.  It also has a nifty flashlight, which is off at the "
"moment."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tactical tonfa (on)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A reinforced plastic tonfa; the core is filled with capacitors and a high-"
"yield rechargeable storage battery.  When a switch on the handle is pressed,"
" a high-voltage current is transmitted to the two electrodes mounted in the "
"end of the weapon, and by extension to anyone unfortunate enough to be in "
"contact with them.  The integral flashlight is turned on, continually "
"draining power and lighting the surrounding area."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "spiked cudgel"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A short bit of wood with nails driven through the business end to create a "
"menacing, if inelegant, weapon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "jitte"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A short steel baton employed by Japanese police in the 17th and 18th "
"century.  A small hook forks from the weapon just above the hilt, intended "
"to aid in snagging or disarming opponents."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "blackjack"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A short, easily concealed bludgeoning weapon consisting of a weight embedded"
" at the end of a short leather shaft.  Formerly used by law enforcement, "
"this weapon is meant to stun or knock out the subject, although head strikes"
" have a high risk of causing a permanent, disabling brain injury or being "
"fatal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "plastic toy cane"
#. ~ Description of variant "plastic villain's cane" of item "plastic toy
#. cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A sinister looking cane made of plastic.  It has a shiny red orb gripped by "
"claws at the handle."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bokken"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A solid wood training katana, exactingly crafted to mimic the weight and "
"balance of the real thing.  Despite its lack of a sharp metal edge, it's "
"still quite capable as a blunt weapon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bowling pin"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A standard bowling pin.  This could make a decent weapon, if it came to "
"that."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bronze mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stick with a lump of bronze at one end.  While not as durable as steel, "
"its heft makes it every bit as effective."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "lump hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout and hefty hammer, more akin to a mini sledge than a claw or ball-"
"peen.  It's useful for portable demolition work, but unwieldy as a weapon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "loaded stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout knotty stick with a large knob at the top that has been left to cure"
" in a chimney.  A traditional Irish weapon, the shillelagh was originally "
"used for settling disputes in a gentlemanly manner.  The knob has been "
"hollowed and filled with molten heavy metal to pack more of a punch."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wooden tonfa"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout wooden truncheon of the sort commonly employed by police.  "
"Originally an Okinawan weapon, it consists of a stick with a perpendicular "
"handle attached a third of the way down its length."
msgstr "一根通常被警察所使用的木製結實短棍。源自沖繩的武器， 由一個握柄垂直連結於棍子的三分之一處所組成。"

#. ~ Description of "shillelagh"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout, knotty stick with a large knob at the top that has been left to "
"cure in a chimney.  A traditional Irish weapon, the shillelagh was "
"originally used for settling disputes in a gentlemanly manner."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "soaking shillelagh"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout, knotty stick with a large knob at the top that is presently soaking"
" in oil.  When it's done, it should be ready to bust some heads."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "baseball bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A sturdy wooden cudgel once essential to the great American pastime."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "expandable baton (extended)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A telescoping baton that's extended and ready to bust some heads.  Activate "
"to collapse."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "expandable baton (collapsed)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A telescoping baton.  Right now, it's collapsed for easy storage.  Activate "
"to expand."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "golf club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A thin aluminum rod with a heavy head on one end for hitting golf balls.  It"
" looks quite fragile, but it could do a fair bit of damage before the shaft "
"got too bent."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "kanabō"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A two-handed war club used in feudal Japan by samurai against armored "
"opponents, it's made from hardwood studded with metal."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "lucerne hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A versatile polearm with a spiked hammer head, a spike, and a hook attached "
"to a beefy wooden pole."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "walking cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A walking stick designed to lean on, whether for mobility assistance or "
"puttin' on the ritz."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wooden crutch"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A wooden rod with a brace designed to help support the body using the arm.  "
"It could be combined with another like it, or used on its own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bō staff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A wooden staff weapon used in Okinawan martial arts.  It has been finely "
"sanded and treated with oil for integrity."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "aluminum crutch"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An aluminum rod with a brace and padding designed to help support the body "
"using the arm.  It could be combined with another like it, or used on its "
"own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "aluminum bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An aluminum version of the tapered club used to play baseball.  It's "
"lighter, stronger, and hits harder than the wooden variety."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "powered quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An ironshod quarterstaff that has a high-voltage stun gun built into the "
"handle.  The stun gun is wired to the metal caps at either end of the staff,"
" allowing you to zap a dangerous opponent should beating them senseless with"
" it prove too hazardous."
msgstr ""

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "expandable baton (extended)"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "telescoping umbrella (extended)"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "travel toilet"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "folded travel toilet"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json data/json/items/tool/misc.json
msgid "Collapse"
msgstr "收回"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "expandable baton (collapsed)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "Expand"
msgstr "伸展"

#. ~ Description of "goedendag"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Halfway between a short spear and a long club, the goedendag consists of a "
"heavy metal spike mounted to the end of an even heavier shaft.  It is "
"unsophisticated, but was once a favorite among medieval infantry who needed "
"a cheap, simple means to smash through enemy armor."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "cudgel"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Mankind's oldest weapon: a length of wood tapered slightly to maximize "
"weight at the business end -- in other words, a club.  This one is quite "
"short, prioritizing speed over power."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "Mjölnir"
msgid_plural "Mjölnirs"
msgstr[0] "雷神錘"

#. ~ Description of "pipe staff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Two steel pipes fitted end-to-end in a clumsy facsimile of a quarterstaff."
msgstr ""

