#. ~ Description of "chain whip"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"A long spool of chain with a steel weight at one end.  What a terrible night"
" it'll be for anyone who gets hit by this thing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "rock in a sock"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"A pair of nested socks with a stone tied inside.  A true weapon of "
"desperation."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "riding crop"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"A rod ending in a leather popper originally used to stimulate a horse and "
"give them orders."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "rope dart"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"A sharp metal spike tied to the end of a long rope, used primarily in "
"Chinese martial arts.  Though often used for show, there's little doubt that"
" a skilled fighter could do real damage with this thing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "horseman's flail"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid "A short pole with a spiked steel ball attached to it by a chain."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "grappling hook"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"A steel hook attached to a long rope.  Deploying this next to a wall might "
"give you a way to climb up."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "war flail"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"A stout pole with a spiked mace head attached to the end with a chain, a "
"purpose-made combat version of the peasant flail.  It specializes in "
"threshing people in metal armor, rather than grain."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "peasant flail"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"A stout pole with a wooden club attached to the end with a leather cord.  "
"This farming tool was historically used to thresh grain, but was frequently "
"pressed into service as a weapon."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "urumi"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"A thin ribbon of flexible steel attached to a handle, the whip sword is an "
"Indian weapon long renowned for its bizarre design and the skill required to"
" properly use it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "bullwhip"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"A very long strip of braided leather with a handle on one end.  Originally "
"developed to settle disagreements with cattle, it's better used now for "
"flaying the rotten flesh off of walking corpses.  Great for when a problem "
"comes along."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "nunchaku"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"A weapon originating from East Asia consisting of a pair of short sticks "
"connected by a shorter rope or chain.  The design is a bit unwieldy, but "
"fast and deadly in the right hands."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "scourge"
#: data/json/items/melee/whips_and_flails.json
msgid ""
"The \"cat 'o nine tails\", a handle with nine short leather whips, each "
"sporting a razor-sharp metal tip.  This ancient instrument of torture can "
"cause bleeding, but by design is inefficient as a weapon."
msgstr ""

