msgstr "驚喜！\"他比了個爵士樂的姿勢。\"抱歉。好吧，之前我被告知我是一個小隊的一員。也許你才是第一個。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thank you for telling me."
msgstr "謝謝你和我說這些。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thanks a lot for having my back.  Like I said, I owe you one."
msgstr "謝謝你幫我。就像我之前說的，我欠你一個人情。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thanks a lot."
msgstr "非常感謝。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Thanks.  I never thought I'd get exhausted of carrying pure gold around, but"
" here we are."
msgstr "謝了。我沒想過有一天我會帶著純金到處走到筋疲力盡，但情況就是如此。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"That's quite the story.  You seem to be feeling pretty good, in spite of the"
" world ending."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"That's what the news said, anyway.  It was only about a 20-minute trip from "
"my apartment and sometimes I'd drive past it, so I was curious and I did "
"some research into it.  The only info I could find about it online said that"
" it was a NASA lab for computer research, but that was probably bullshit.  I"
" mean, do you see any NASA logos?  Sure, we got huge steel doors and 15-foot"
" concrete walls, but not a logo in sight.  The building probably goes "
"underground, right?  It's way too small to be a whole laboratory up here."
msgstr ""
"不管怎樣，新聞是這麼說的。從我公寓到這邊大概20分鐘路程，有時候我開車會經過，所以我很好奇並查閱了一些資訊。我在網路上唯一能找到的資訊是，這是NASA的電腦研究實驗室，當然那可能只是掩飾。我是說，你有看到任何NASA的標誌嗎？當然，這裡有扇15英尺高的混凝土牆，但沒有標誌。這建築可能是蓋在地下的，是吧？這裡太小了，不太可能是個完整的實驗室。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Then the portals happened, and you know the rest from there.  Two days "
"later, the world was over.  There was a lot of chaos in my complex.  I just "
"nailed shut my front door, drew all the curtains, kept my shotgun loaded, "
"and probably slept maybe ten hours total that week.  I don't know if there "
"was someone up in the sky watching over me, but if there was, I sure as hell"
" owe them big time."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "They don't let you in to sleep?"
msgstr "他們不讓你進去睡覺？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thinking I should go hunt something soon…"
msgstr "我想我應該盡快去獵點東西..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Uh… okay.  Who are you?"
msgstr "呃...好吧。你是誰？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Want help with something else?"
msgstr "需要其他幫助嗎？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Want help with something?"
msgstr "需要些幫忙嗎？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Well, I should get going."
msgstr "好吧，我應該走了。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Well, never mind."
msgstr "好吧，沒關係。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Well, no.  It was obvious they just wanted to get rid of me, but I decided I wanted to show that I was useful.  They tell me to find a crashed drone somewhere in the surrounding area and bring it back here.  No directions, of course.  Y'know, go find this drone in the middle of the woods, it'll be easy.  But I had some tools in my bag, right?  And yours truly has repaired some drones in the park service.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"So it takes me a whole-ass afternoon, but I find their stupid drone stuck in a tree.  I can see the camera's still on, so I pick it up and I tell the lens: 'Hey, you want me to fix it too?'  And I do.  It was just a cracked frame and the wiring to the rotors was sliced up.  The propellers themselves were fine.  So I bring it out of the woods and turn it off.  Then I open up the casing, solder up the wires, and use superglue to hold the frame together, which wasn't perfect, but I figured it'd hold until it got back home.  Then I turned it back on, and wouldn't you know, it immediately starts up and sits there for a minute, like 'What the fuck?  Why am I working again?'  And then it flies away, and I walk my smug ass back home."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Well, thanks for offering."
msgstr "好吧，謝謝你的提議。"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Well… a little while ago, I set up a radio transmitter in the radio tower "
"not far from here, but apparently it's stopped transmitting.  If you're "
"willing to back me up while I check it out, I'll owe you a favor."
msgstr "好吧...不久前，我在離這裡不遠的無線電塔安裝了一個無線電發射器，但顯然它已經停止工作了。如果你願意在我檢查時幫我一把，我欠你一個人情。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "What do you know about our employers?"
msgstr "你對我們的雇主了解多少？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "What food were you canning?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "What was <the_cataclysm> like for you?"
msgstr "對你來說<the_cataclysm>是怎麼樣的？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Who are you, exactly?"
msgstr "你到底是誰？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Who exactly are you?"
msgstr "你到底是誰？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Whoo-ee, someone was living under a rock, huh?  It was all over the news.  "
"Video on YouTube, it was a livestream of one of the riots in Minneapolis.  A"
" mom was…\"  They hesitate.  \"I don't want to go into detail, but it was "
"real bad.  Real bad.  That's what set off people panicking."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of mission "Return to Hub 01"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"With the source of the radio tower's interference fixed, return to Hub 01 "
"with Cranberry."
msgstr "解決了無線電塔的干擾原後，帶著Cranberry回到 Hub 01 基地。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Wondering if the whole world is like this now.  It has to be, right?  I was "
"watching some foreign news channels when everything was going down, and it "
"sounded like things were just as bad there…"
msgstr "我也想知道現在是否整個世界都變得這樣了。應該是吧？我之前一切都變變糟看過一些國外的新聞頻道，聽起來情況都一樣遭。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Yeah!  Crazy shit.  They sent me to an office building to find a folder with"
" a certain serial and get rid of it.  They didn't even care what was on it."
"  By the time I got there, though, the building was pretty much a wreck.  "
"The folder had been sitting in a puddle for God knows how long, and there "
"was nothing even remotely legible by then."
msgstr ""
"是阿！見鬼的任務。他們派我去一棟辦公大樓，找到某個特定序號的文件夾銷毀它。他們甚至不在乎上面寫什麼。然而，當我到達那兒的時候，那建築幾乎已經是廢墟。文件夾早就不知道泡在水裡多久，上面根本看不清任何東西。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Yeah.  Have you noticed how they pay us in these tiny little gold coins?\"  "
"Cranberry holds one up for emphasis.  \"It's bizarre.  You'd think they have"
" a gold mine in there, but no, they don't, so they make me cross the damn "
"world grabbing gold bars.  As far as scrip goes, it seems inconvenient as "
"hell to make."
msgstr ""
"是阿。你有注意到那些他們付給我們的小小金幣了嗎？\"Cranberry拿起其中一個並強調。\"這可真是奇怪。你會以為他們有座金礦呢，但不是，他們沒有金礦，所以他們派我翻遍這該死的世界來找金條給他們。單就做為代幣而言，這些製造起來似乎難度相當大。"

